Enrichment Factor (FE) is used to defferentiate between natural and anthropogenic metals. Msed = metal concentration and Mc = metal concentration in the Earth’s crust (Taylor and McLennan 1995; McLennan 2001).\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$FE=\frac{\left(\frac{{M}_{sed}}{{Al}_{sed}}\right)}{\left(\frac{{M}_{c}}{{Al}_{c}}\right)}$$\end{document}

Geoacumulation index (Igeo) is the metal pollution index where Cn is the metal concentration in sediments, Bn is the background concentration of the metal (the same used for EF) Factor 1.5 is the background matrix correction factor due to lithospheric effects (Müller 1969)\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${I}_{geo}={log}_{2}\left(\frac{{C}_{n}}{{1.5B}_{n}}\right)$$\end{document}

Ecological risk potential, evaluates the probable risk as result of metal pollution, were i = metal, Tri is the biological toxicity factor for a given element (i), Cf, Cs and Cn = contamination factor, metal concentration in sediments and the background value respectively, IR = is the sum of Rei for several metals (Hakanson 1980).\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ {{RE}}_{{{f}}}^{{{i}}} = {{Tr}}^{{{i}}} {{xC}}_{{{f}}}^{{{i}}} = {{Tr}}^{{{i}}} {{x}}\left( {\frac{{{{C}}_{{{s}}}^{{{i}}} }}{{{{C}}_{{{n}}}^{{{i}}} }}} \right)\quad {{IR}} = \mathop \sum \limits_{{{f}}}^{{{i}}} {{RE}}_{{{f}}}^{{{i}}} $$\end{document}
